---
import AppLayout from "@/layouts/AppLayout.astro";
import { getAllApps } from "@/lib/apps";
const entry = (await getAllApps()).find(({ data }) => data.slug === "movecut");
if (!entry) throw new Error("MoveCut app entry is missing.");
const app = entry.data;
---

<AppLayout
  app={app}
  locale="en"
  title="MoveCut Support"
  description="Help with MoveCut photos, permissions, saving, sharing, local data, purchases, and support requests."
  canonical="/movecut/support/"
>
  <div class="shell legal-shell">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/movecut/">MoveCut</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span
        >Support</span
      >
    </nav>
    <header class="legal-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">MoveCut help</p>
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p>Help with photos, permissions, saving, sharing, and purchases.</p>
      <div class="legal-meta">
        <span>MoveCut 1.3.0</span><span>English and Korean</span>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="legal-grid">
      <aside class="legal-sidebar">
        <nav aria-label="On this page">
          <h2>On this page</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
            <li><a href="#photos">Photos and permissions</a></li>
            <li><a href="#saving">Saving and sharing</a></li>
            <li><a href="#data">Local data and deletion</a></li>
            <li><a href="#purchase">Purchase and reinstall</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>
        <a href="/movecut/privacy/en/">Privacy Policy →</a>
      </aside>
      <article class="legal-content">
        <h2 id="contact">1. Contact MoveCut support</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href="mailto:c335544@gmail.com?subject=MoveCut%20Support"
            >c335544@gmail.com</a
          >. Include your device model, iOS or Android version, MoveCut version,
          what you expected, and the steps that caused the issue.
        </p>
        <p>
          Do not attach personal workout photos unless they are necessary to
          explain the problem. MoveCut has no account system, so support will
          never ask for a password or verification code.
        </p>

        <h2 id="photos">2. Photos and permissions</h2>
        <p>
          MoveCut asks for camera access only when you choose to take a photo.
          Choosing an existing image uses your operating system’s photo picker.
          Saving a finished card may require permission to add an image to
          Photos.
        </p>
        <p>
          If access was denied, open your device Settings, find MoveCut, and
          allow Camera or Photos access for the feature you want to use. The app
          does not require microphone, contacts, precise location, or tracking
          permission.
        </p>

        <h2 id="saving">3. Saving and sharing</h2>
        <p>
          “Save to My Cards” keeps an editable record inside MoveCut. “Save to
          Photos” writes a finished PNG to your photo library. “Share” opens the
          system share sheet and sends the finished image only to the app you
          choose.
        </p>
        <p>
          If saving fails, confirm that your device has free storage and that
          MoveCut can add photos. If sharing fails, try saving to Photos first
          and share the saved image from the Photos app.
        </p>

        <h2 id="data">4. Local data, backup, and deletion</h2>
        <p>
          MoveCut stores photos and workout details locally and does not provide
          an operator-run cloud account or cross-device sync. Delete a saved
          entry from My Cards to remove that app record. Files already saved to
          Photos must be deleted separately in Photos.
        </p>
        <p>
          Deleting the app or clearing app data can remove your MoveCut library.
          Device backups may behave differently depending on your iCloud,
          Google, device, and operating system settings. Save important finished
          cards to Photos before deleting or changing devices.
        </p>

        <h2 id="purchase">5. Purchase, reinstall, and refund help</h2>
        <p>
          MoveCut is sold as a one-time paid download. There is no subscription
          or in-app purchase. Store billing, receipts, refunds, and download
          access are managed by the App Store or Google Play account used for
          the purchase.
        </p>
        <p>
          To reinstall, sign in to the same store account and download MoveCut
          from your purchase history when it remains available for your device
          and region. A reinstall does not guarantee restoration of cards stored
          only inside the app.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a href="https://support.apple.com/billing"
              >Apple purchase and billing support</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/workflow/9813244"
              >Google Play refund help</a>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Read the <a href="/movecut/privacy/en/">MoveCut Privacy Policy</a> for details
          about local storage, permissions, sharing, backups, retention, and support
          emails.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</AppLayout>
